{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "expand-fueltype-diesel-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.5 step 7d, the SOURCE TYPE dimension at its smallest discriminating width: the `expand-fueltype-diesel` run computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE through `moves-onroad.esm`. It selects two source types, 21 (passenger car) and 32 (light commercial truck), and is otherwise `process-tirewear`'s scope with `expand-day`'s pollutant-processes.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES, which §23 asks for before a dimension is called covered.\n\n* THE SOURCE TYPE AS AN AXIS, AND THE VEHICLE UNDER IT. Every other RunSpec in this tree selects one source type, so until 7d a model that summed `runspecsourcetype` into a scalar passed the whole suite -- and one did: `run_sourceTypeID` was exactly that sum. The drive cycle is the deep half, and it goes one key further than the source type. Vehicle-specific power is computed from a row of `sourceusetypephysics`, which is keyed by (sourceTypeID, regClassID, model-year range): source type 21 has one such row and source type 32 has three -- regulatory class 30, and regulatory class 41 split at model year 2010 because its fixed mass factor changes from 2.05979 to 5.0. So this run computes FOUR drive cycles, not two, and the operating-mode distribution a rate row is weighted by is its own vehicle's. A model that had one per source type got source type 32 wrong by between 1.48 and 3.06 in every cell and by 1.157 in the pollutant total; nothing narrower than this document could see it.\n\n* A COHORT COUNT THAT IS A SUM AND NOT A PRODUCT. 248 rows, not 250: source type 21 carries 125 surviving (modelYearID, fuelTypeID) cohorts and source type 32 carries 123. Both select the same four fuels, so the difference is in `samplevehiclepopulation` -- two candidates have no sample vehicle and are not emitted. Nothing in the model declares 248. `runspecsourcefueltype` is the cohort grid's second factor and carries (sourceTypeID, fuelTypeID) PAIRS, `coh_rank` densifies whatever survives, and `cohortSurvivorCount` recomputes the total, so the ragged count arrives as one number that the shape check holds the emitted relation to.\n\nTHE TEN SELECTIONS, ONE BINDING AND THE ORACLE are everything this document carries. Against `runspecs/expand-day.esm` it differs in eleven `url_template`s and nothing else -- same binding, same structure -- which is the measurement PLAN.md §7.1 wanted: a second source type costs a per-fixture document nothing, because the cost was paid once in the domain model.\n\nWHAT IT REPRODUCES, as of 2026-09-18. All 248 rows of `MOVESOutput`, worst cell 7.372e-06 against a 2e-05 tolerance and worst per-pollutant emissionQuant sum 2.000e-08. It was in `runspecs/pending/` for two days and for two different reasons, and both are now measured rather than waited on: the source bin (PLAN.md §7.3.6) and the physics row (§7.3.7). Every factor of an emission is checked against something the run itself recorded -- the source-hour activity against the execution database's own `sho`, the source-bin distribution against its own `sourceBinDistributionFuelUsage_1_26161_2020` at 330 bins with every per-(source type, model year) total exactly 1, including the fuel-usage re-attribution that moves 98.2% of equipped E85 into gasoline -- so the agreement is four right factors and not four errors that cancel.\n\nTHE SHAPE IS RECOMPUTED AND NOT DECLARED, which is the other half of what this document holds the chain to. 248 rows, 125 under source type 21 and 123 under 32: `n_outputCohort` is declared in the binding and `cohortSurvivorCount` recomputes it from the chain, and `tools/check-runspec-shape.py` asserts the two against the emitted keys. The same check covers the two WIDTHS this run needs above their defaults -- `n_sourceBin` 2 and `n_physicsRow` 4 -- through `run_sourceBinsDropped`, `run_physicsRowsDropped` and `run_rateRowsWithoutPhysics`, all three of which are zero here. Those are a different kind of check from the row count: a width one short does not lose a row, it loses a term of one, and the row count would not notice.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "expand-day"
    ]
  },
